  "description": "The shape of the specification's own Examples (lines 1104-1116): a transferable indexed signature groups code (-X) whose group holds a prefix (E), a sequence number (0A), a digest (E) and a controller signature group (-K) of two signatures. -X's size, 73 (11 + 6 + 11 + 1 + 44), counts every quadlet including -K's code and contents; -K's is 44. The specification's example is built the same way: -XBf is 95 = 11 + 6 + 11 + 1 + 66. The symbol legends of the Encoding Scheme Symbols Table (line 674) and the indexed-code symbol table (line 714), and the Examples text at line 1103, say a count code's digits count 'Primitives or groups'; this case rests on the explicit rule at line 591 instead and records the others in spec_conflicts.",
